{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba apps/site/content/docs/agentic-dev/tool-exec.mdx'","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: tool-exec\n     3\tdescription: Governed tool-call / sandboxed-exec primitive, a default-deny command allowlist, Zod-strict argv validation, and execFile arg-arrays only, never a shell.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t`@caisson/tool-exec` is the security floor Agentic-Dev's tool layer stands on: a governed gate\n     7\tbetween an agent's tool call and a real process spawn. A call names a registered logical command;\n     8\tanything unregistered is refused before anything spawns.\n     9\t\n    10\t## What it does\n    11\t\n    12\t- **Default-deny command allowlist.** `createToolExec({ allowlist })`: an empty or absent\n    13\t  allowlist refuses every call, fail-closed. An unregistered name throws `NotFoundError` before a\n    14\t  process is spawned.\n    15\t- **`execFile` arg-arrays only.** Never `execSync`/`exec`/`shell: true`, never a concatenated\n    16\t  command string. Each registered command declares a real executable plus a Zod-`.strict()`\n    17\t  schema its args must satisfy; args are validated with `parseStrict` and the validated result\n    18\t  becomes the exact argv array passed to `execFile`: no agent-supplied value ever reaches a shell.\n    19\t- **Structured argument provenance.** Every call returns `{ command, args, exitCode, stdout,\n    20\t  stderr, ok, reason?, at }`, a plain-data audit record, output bounded to 64KB. A non-zero exit\n    21\t  resolves in the record rather than throwing; only an unregistered name or a schema failure throws.\n    22\t- **Everything injected.** `cwd`, `timeoutMs`, the spawn seam (`execFn`), and the clock (`now`) are\n    23\t  all config, no module-level secrets or constants for endpoints or executables.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Install\n    26\t\n    27\t```bash\n    28\tbun add @caisson/tool-exec\n    29\t```\n    30\t\n    31\t## Quickstart\n    32\t\n    33\t```ts\n    34\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n    35\timport { createToolExec } from \"@caisson/tool-exec\";\n    36\t\n    37\tconst toolExec = createToolExec({\n    38\t  allowlist: [\n    39\t    {\n    40\t      name: \"git-status\",\n    41\t      command: \"/usr/bin/git\",\n    42\t      argsSchema: z.array(z.string()).max(1).default([\"status\"]),\n    43\t    },\n    44\t  ],\n    45\t  cwd: \"/repo\",\n    46\t  timeoutMs: 30_000,\n    47\t});\n    48\t\n    49\tconst result = await toolExec.run(\"git-status\", [\"status\"], \"agent-turn-14\");\n    50\t// result.ok / result.exitCode / result.stdout / result.args (the resolved argv array)\n    51\t```\n    52\t\n    53\tA name not on the allowlist, or args that fail the schema, throw before any process spawns.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Configuration\n    56\t\n    57\t`ToolExecConfig`:\n    58\t\n    59\t- `allowlist: CommandSpec[]`: required. Each entry is `{ name, command, argsSchema }`.\n    60\t- `cwd?: string`: defaults to `process.cwd()`.\n    61\t- `timeoutMs?: number`: defaults to `30_000`.\n    62\t- `execFn?: ExecFn`: inject a spawn double for tests; defaults to a real `execFile` call.\n    63\t- `now?: () => number`: inject a clock for testable provenance timestamps; defaults to `Date.now`.\n    64\t\n    65\t## Composition\n    66\t\n    67\t`tool-exec` depends on `@caisson/kernel` for `NotFoundError` and `parseStrict`: the same\n    68\tdefault-deny and schema-validation primitives the rest of the base substrate uses, so a tool call's\n    69\tfailure modes look like every other kernel-governed boundary. It's the gate Agentic-Dev's agent\n    70\tkernel and agent-runner reach for whenever a running agent needs to touch a real executable.\n    71\t\n    72\t<Callout type=\"info\" title=\"Commercial, Agentic-Dev\">\n    73\t  `@caisson/tool-exec` ships under the Agentic-Dev bundle license.\n    74\t</Callout>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
